<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Świna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Świna (German: Swine) is a strait in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> connecting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Szczecin</a> Lagoon with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a> between the islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usedom">Usedom</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolin">Wolin</a>. The port of Świnoujście stands at its mouth, and it carries the main shipping channel to Szczecin. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peene">Peene</a> and the Dziwna it forms one of the three outlets of the Oder to the sea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swina.jpg" alt="Świna" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Specjal b · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swinoujscie_30.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
